  "body": "Unlock Potential on Rukutai Street - 1186sqm (approx.) Land, rebuild or renovate\r\n\r\nPositioned in one of Auckland's most tightly held bayside suburbs, 75A Rukutai Street, Orakei presents a compelling opportunity to secure a foothold in an enviable Eastern Suburbs location.\r\n\r\nWhether you are looking to renovate, rebuild, or landbank (subject to council approval), this property offers the space, zoning, and address to reward vision and add real value. Set on a generous parcel in the Residential - Mixed Housing Suburban Zone, the existing 1940s home features six bedrooms in two dwellings 200sqm floor area (approx.) and ample off-street parking, providing comfortable accommodation while you plan your next move.\r\n\r\nLifestyle & Location Highlights:\r\n\r\nCoastal Convenience: Minutes from the golden sands of Mission Bay, Okahu Bay, and the Tamaki Drive waterfront promenade.\r\n\r\nEveryday Essentials: Close to Eastridge Shopping Centre, local cafes, restaurants, and scenic walkways around Orakei Basin.\r\n\r\nEasy Commuting: Seamless access to Auckland CBD, public transport links, and Orakei Train Station.\r\n\r\nSought-After Schooling: Zoned for Orakei School and Selwyn College, with easy access to leading private schools.\r\n\r\nProperties in this blue-chip pocket of Orakei are always in high demand. Act decisively to secure your place in this premier coastal neighbourhood.\r\n\r\nAuction: Thursday, 10th Dec at 1:00 pm (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nVenue: Ray White Auction Room, 272 Parnell Road, Parnell\r\n\r\nOpen homes: Saturday and Sunday 1:00-1:30pm or view by appointment\r\n\r\nContact George Erdos 021 959 331, Howard Sidnam 021 973 389 or Sharon Lee 027 443 1368",
